# SysPlex — Docker build context
#
# Allowlist, not denylist. Everything is excluded, then the eight paths the
# Dockerfile actually COPYs are added back.
#
# A denylist was tried before (Docker/.dockerignore) and failed the way
# denylists do: it never mentioned the agent binaries or vendored DLLs, so every build shipped
# 24 MB of Go binaries and 1.6 MB of .NET DLLs to the daemon, plus a 23 MB .git
# directory. It also sat in Docker/, where the daemon never looks — the context
# root is the only place a .dockerignore is read.
#
# Keep this in sync with the COPY lines in the Dockerfile. If a build fails on
# a missing file, the fix is a new `!` line here, not a switch back to a denylist.

# Exclude everything.
*

# Re-include only what the build needs.
!requirements.txt
!server/
!docker-entrypoint.sh

# Re-exclude generated and local files that live inside the allowed paths.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.backup
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

